{"entry":{"id":"l-ca9317c6385dd6cf","lemma":"صَدَّ","root":"صدد","arabic":"لَيَصُدُّونَهُمْ","gloss":"surely, turn them","transliteration":"layaṣuddūnahum","representativeKey":"43:37:2","exampleKeys":["43:37:2","43:62:2","47:1:3"],"occurrenceCount":37,"courseOrder":292,"sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"],"rootId":"r-8855b2c809966664","approval":{"status":"pending"}},"examples":[{"ref":"43:37","tokens":[{"key":"43:37:1","position":1,"arabic":"وَإِنَّهُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"And indeed, they","transliteration":"wa-innahum","lemma":"إِنّ","root":null,"entryId":"l-3afba549abbd5639"},{"key":"43:37:2","position":2,"arabic":"لَيَصُدُّونَهُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"surely, turn them","transliteration":"layaṣuddūnahum","lemma":"صَدَّ","root":"صدد","entryId":"l-ca9317c6385dd6cf"},{"key":"43:37:3","position":3,"arabic":"عَنِ","kind":"word","gloss":"from","transliteration":"ʿani","lemma":"عَن","root":null,"entryId":"l-f1109a78c8548754"},{"key":"43:37:4","position":4,"arabic":"ٱلسَّبِيلِ","kind":"word","gloss":"the Path","transliteration":"l-sabīli","lemma":"سَبِيل","root":"سبل","entryId":"l-c204df14296b43ea"},{"key":"43:37:5","position":5,"arabic":"وَيَحْسَبُونَ","kind":"word","gloss":"and they think","transliteration":"wayaḥsabūna","lemma":"حَسِبَ","root":"حسب","entryId":"l-717e0311dc7803f9"},{"key":"43:37:6","position":6,"arabic":"أَنَّهُم","kind":"word","gloss":"that they","transliteration":"annahum","lemma":"أَنّ","root":null,"entryId":"l-9a8e074398908017"},{"key":"43:37:7","position":7,"arabic":"مُّهْتَدُونَ","kind":"word","gloss":"(are) guided","transliteration":"muh'tadūna","lemma":"مُّهْتَدُون","root":"هدي","entryId":null},{"key":"43:37:8","position":8,"arabic":"٣٧","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"And verily, they (Satans / devils) hinder them from the Path (of Allâh), but they think that they are guided aright!","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"targetKey":"43:37:2","targetGloss":"surely, turn them","targetTransliteration":"layaṣuddūnahum","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]},{"ref":"43:62","tokens":[{"key":"43:62:1","position":1,"arabic":"وَلَا","kind":"word","gloss":"And (let) not","transliteration":"walā","lemma":"لَا","root":null,"entryId":"l-93952243ccc22536"},{"key":"43:62:2","position":2,"arabic":"يَصُدَّنَّكُمُ","kind":"word","gloss":"avert you","transliteration":"yaṣuddannakumu","lemma":"صَدَّ","root":"صدد","entryId":"l-ca9317c6385dd6cf"},{"key":"43:62:3","position":3,"arabic":"ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنُ ۖ","kind":"word","gloss":"the Shaitaan","transliteration":"l-shayṭānu","lemma":"شَيْطَٰن","root":"شطن","entryId":"l-1edf2a3c0afdde81"},{"key":"43:62:4","position":4,"arabic":"إِنَّهُۥ","kind":"word","gloss":"Indeed, he","transliteration":"innahu","lemma":"إِنّ","root":null,"entryId":"l-3afba549abbd5639"},{"key":"43:62:5","position":5,"arabic":"لَكُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"(is) for you","transliteration":"lakum","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null},{"key":"43:62:6","position":6,"arabic":"عَدُوٌّۭ","kind":"word","gloss":"an enemy","transliteration":"ʿaduwwun","lemma":"عَدُوّ","root":"عدو","entryId":"l-f920590bc8ef63e8"},{"key":"43:62:7","position":7,"arabic":"مُّبِينٌۭ","kind":"word","gloss":"clear","transliteration":"mubīnun","lemma":"مُّبِين","root":"بين","entryId":"l-0d597777bd2bba00"},{"key":"43:62:8","position":8,"arabic":"٦٢","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"And let not Shaitân (Satan) hinder you (from the right religion, i.e. Islâmic Monotheism). Verily, he (Satan) to you is a plain enemy.","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"targetKey":"43:62:2","targetGloss":"avert you","targetTransliteration":"yaṣuddannakumu","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]},{"ref":"47:1","tokens":[{"key":"47:1:1","position":1,"arabic":"ٱلَّذِينَ","kind":"word","gloss":"Those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","lemma":"الَّذِى","root":null,"entryId":"l-5016cb590bd9088a"},{"key":"47:1:2","position":2,"arabic":"كَفَرُوا۟","kind":"word","gloss":"disbelieve","transliteration":"kafarū","lemma":"كَفَرَ","root":"كفر","entryId":"l-f6f8e55e4806177f"},{"key":"47:1:3","position":3,"arabic":"وَصَدُّوا۟","kind":"word","gloss":"and turn away","transliteration":"waṣaddū","lemma":"صَدَّ","root":"صدد","entryId":"l-ca9317c6385dd6cf"},{"key":"47:1:4","position":4,"arabic":"عَن","kind":"word","gloss":"from","transliteration":"ʿan","lemma":"عَن","root":null,"entryId":"l-f1109a78c8548754"},{"key":"47:1:5","position":5,"arabic":"سَبِيلِ","kind":"word","gloss":"(the) way of Allah","transliteration":"sabīli","lemma":"سَبِيل","root":"سبل","entryId":"l-c204df14296b43ea"},{"key":"47:1:6","position":6,"arabic":"ٱللَّهِ","kind":"word","gloss":"(the) way of Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","lemma":"اللَّه","root":"اله","entryId":"l-4b28e3627200a6c3"},{"key":"47:1:7","position":7,"arabic":"أَضَلَّ","kind":"word","gloss":"He will cause to be lost","transliteration":"aḍalla","lemma":"أَضَلَّ","root":"ضلل","entryId":"l-73112703ea29a8c7"},{"key":"47:1:8","position":8,"arabic":"أَعْمَـٰلَهُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"their deeds","transliteration":"aʿmālahum","lemma":"عَمَل","root":"عمل","entryId":"l-794a9256c242f950"},{"key":"47:1:9","position":9,"arabic":"١","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}],"translation":"Those who disbelieve (in the Oneness of Allâh, and in the Message of Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم), and hinder (men) from the Path of Allâh (Islâmic Monotheism), He will render their deeds vain.","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[{"text":"It is obligatory to have Belief in the Messengership of the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. Narrated Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه: Allâh’s Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم said, \"By Him (Allâh) in Whose Hand Muhammad’s soul is, there is none from amongst the Jews and the Christians (of these present nations) who hears about me and then dies without believing in the Message with which I have been sent (i.e. Islâmic Monotheism), but he will be from the dwellers of the (Hell) Fire.\" (Sahih Muslim , the Book of Faith, Vol.1, Chapter No.240). See also (V.3:85) and (V.3:116).","ref":null}],"targetKey":"47:1:3","targetGloss":"and turn away","targetTransliteration":"waṣaddū","sourceIds":["qul-56","qul-92","qul-71","qul-75","qul-76","qul-301"]}]}